  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "The air is thin and we have to rest several times on the short hike from camp. To our left, snow-covered mountains disappear into clouds that seem almost close enough to touch.",
      "cn": "空气很稀薄，在从营地出发的短途徒步中我们不得不休息几次。在我们的左方，白雪覆盖的山脉消失在云层中，那云层似乎近得几乎触手可及。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "On the {plain} in front of us, we can just make out a {herd} of graceful animals. This is why we're here—to {observe} Tibetan antelopes.",
      "cn": "在我们面前的一片平原上，我们隐约辨认出一群体形优美的动物。这正是我们来到此地的原因——观察藏羚羊。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "Tibetan antelopes live on the plains of Tibet, Xinjiang, and Qinghai. Watching them move slowly across the green grass, I'm struck by their {beauty}.",
      "cn": "藏羚羊生活在西藏、新疆和青海的平原上。看着它们缓缓地穿过绿草，我被它们的美丽所打动。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "I'm also reminded of the danger they are in. They are being hunted, {illegally}, for their valuable {fur}.",
      "cn": "我也想到了它们所处的危险。它们因其珍贵的皮毛而正遭到非法猎杀。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "My guide is Zhaxi, a villager from Changtang. He works at the Changtang National Nature {Reserve}. The {reserve} is a shelter for the animals and plants of northwestern Tibet.",
      "cn": "我的向导是扎西，一位来自羌塘的村民。他在羌塘国家级自然保护区工作。该保护区是西藏西北部动植物的庇护所。"
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "To Zhaxi, the land is {sacred} and protecting the wildlife is a way of life. \"We're not trying to save the animals,\" he says. \"Actually, we're trying to save ourselves.\"",
      "cn": "对扎西而言，这片土地是神圣的，保护野生生物就是一种生活方式。\"我们并不是要去拯救动物，\"他说，\"实际上，我们是在拯救我们自己。\""
    },
    {
      "num": "07",
      "en": "The 1980s and 1990s were bad times for the Tibetan {antelope}. The population dropped by more than 50 percent. Hunters were shooting antelopes to make profits. Their habitats were becoming smaller as new roads and railways were built.",
      "cn": "20世纪80年代和90年代对藏羚羊来说是一段糟糕的时期。藏羚羊的数量减少了50%以上。猎人们为了牟利而射杀藏羚羊。随着新的公路和铁路的修建，它们的栖息地正变得越来越小。"
    },
    {
      "num": "08",
      "en": "In order to save this {species} from {extinction}, the Chinese government placed it under national protection. Zhaxi and other volunteers watched over the antelopes day and night to keep them safe from attacks.",
      "cn": "为了使这一物种免遭灭绝，中国政府将其纳入国家保护。扎西和其他志愿者日夜守护着藏羚羊，使它们免受袭击。"
    },
    {
      "num": "09",
      "en": "Bridges and gates were added to let the antelopes move easily and keep them safe from cars and trains.",
      "cn": "人们架起了桥梁、增设了闸门，让藏羚羊能够轻松迁徙，并保护它们免受汽车和列车的伤害。"
    },
    {
      "num": "10",
      "en": "The measures were {effective}. The {antelope} population has recovered and in June 2015, the Tibetan {antelope} was removed from the endangered {species} list.",
      "cn": "这些措施是有效的。藏羚羊的数量已经恢复，并且在2015年6月，藏羚羊被从濒危物种名单中移除。"
    },
    {
      "num": "11",
      "en": "The government, however, does not {intend} to stop the protection programmes, since the threats to the Tibetan {antelope} have not yet disappeared.",
      "cn": "然而，由于对藏羚羊的威胁尚未消失，政府并不打算停止这些保护项目。"
    },
    {
      "num": "12",
      "en": "In the evening, I drink a cup of tea and watch the stars. I think about the antelopes and what Zhaxi told me. Much is being done to protect wildlife, but if we really want to save the planet, we must change our way of life.",
      "cn": "傍晚，我喝着一杯茶，望着星星。我想着藏羚羊，想着扎西对我所说的话。为了保护野生动物，我们已经做了很多，但如果我们真的想拯救地球，就必须改变我们的生活方式。"
    },
    {
      "num": "13",
      "en": "Only when we learn to {exist} in {harmony} with nature can we stop being a {threat} to wildlife and to our planet.",
      "cn": "只有当我们学会与大自然和谐共存时，我们才不会成为野生生物和地球的威胁。"
    }
  ],
